<p>Spain has released previously secret documents from an official investigation into the failed 23 February 1981 coup attempt, on the same day Antonio Tejero Molina—the Civil Guard officer who led the seizure of parliament—died at 93. The newly published batch includes 153 documents, which outlets said cover both the coup attempt and the inquiry that followed. Tejero became the enduring image of 23-F when television cameras captured him entering Congress with a pistol and ordering lawmakers to the floor as armed officers held the chamber.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3CpqhCkmHGOwZHppMVgNzx22D2m91vuOz8-8p24D2IBlvnn8l3XsbGy4-NdvKqwwnDBjoMUCFHmr3NP5sDHtD3B58U1MmiTQqfIp00nRrs3SHVfsnrJpfeKRZKN2CYoURei_5STNy30Zbm__R-OaqLWUNXWcpO8a9fV2zfUvHhnwZRmTH_2o61_7hEcZEI53' alt='Lt. Col. Antonio Tejero Molina, with a pistol in his hand, attempting a coup at the Spanish Parliament on Feb. 23, 1981.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Government rationale: Officials said opening the archive should help clarify what happened and dispel long-running conspiracy theories about 23-F.</li><li>Why it’s notable now: The release comes 45 years after the coup attempt and draws on an investigation file that stayed secret for decades.</li><li>Level of force contemplated: Euronews said the documents refer to orders to “shoot to kill,” a stark sign of how far some plotters were prepared to go.</li><li>Why the coup collapsed: Coverage of the investigation material says the putsch fell apart without broad backing from Spain’s armed forces.</li><li>Political milieu: The Guardian cast Tejero as part of a wider rightwing network of police and military officers involved in the plot.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Spanish government: Officials framed the declassification as a transparency measure intended to clarify what happened and help dispel conspiracy theories about 23-F. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce8w42e152xo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Euronews (document reporting): Euronews highlighted that the declassified materials include references to “shoot to kill” orders, underscoring the seriousness of the plans described in the archive. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/25/spain-releases-secret-1981-coup-documents-after-45-years'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>The Guardian (historical framing): The Guardian described Tejero as part of a rightwing network of police and military officers and stressed that Juan Carlos’s refusal to support the plot helped thwart it. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/25/spanish-officer-led-1981-coup-dies-day-documents-declassified-antonio-tejero'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>The New York Times (investigation focus): The New York Times said the publication of long-secret investigation files aims to end decades of conjecture about why the coup failed. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/25/world/europe/spain-coup-1981-files-revealed.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/antonio-tejero-franco-loyalist-and-leader-of-spains-failed-1981-coup-dies-at-93'>Antonio Tejero, Franco loyalist and leader of Spain&#x27;s failed 1981 coup, dies at 93</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/25/spain-releases-secret-1981-coup-documents-after-45-years'>Spain releases secret 1981 coup documents after 45 years</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce8w42e152xo'>Spain declassifies files on 1981 attempted coup in effort to dispel conspiracy theories</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/25/world/europe/spain-coup-1981-files-revealed.html'>45 Years After Failed Coup, Spain Declassifies Files About Why It Failed</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rejmwo/spain_declassifies_files_on_1981_attempted_coup/'>Spain declassifies files on 1981 attempted coup</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/25/spanish-officer-led-1981-coup-dies-day-documents-declassified-antonio-tejero'>Spanish officer who led 1981 coup dies on day documents declassified</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>